-- title:
--   Vectors in an archimedean cut are K_∞¹-finite
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a number field and let $\mathrm{tys}$ be an archimedean type family for $F$, that is, a natural number $\mathrm{card}(w)$ for each infinite place $w$ of $F$ together with, for each $w$ and each index $i \in \{0,\dots,\mathrm{card}(w)-1\}$, a datum $\mathrm{rep}\,w\,i$ consisting of a dimension $n$ and a complex representation of the group `rowIsometrySubgroup₀` of the completion $F_w$ on $\mathbb{C}^n$. Let $f$ be a complex-valued function on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F)$, the general linear group of $2\times 2$ matrices over the adele ring of $F$, and suppose $f$ lies in the archimedean cut submodule of $\mathrm{tys}$, i.e. in the infimum over all infinite places $w$ of the supremum over $i$ of the submodules `typeSubmodule` attached to the group homomorphism `rowIsometryInclAt₀ F w` into $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F)$ and to the representation component of $\mathrm{rep}\,w\,i$ (so that at every place $w$ the function $f$ belongs to the sum of the finitely many listed type pieces at $w$). Then the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the set of functions of the form $x \mapsto f(xk)$, where $k$ ranges over the subgroup of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F)$ generated by the ranges of the homomorphisms `rowIsometryInclAt₀ F w` for all infinite places $w$, is finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{C}$.
--
--   This is the $K$-finiteness of vectors cut out by prescribed archimedean types: a function whose behaviour at each infinite place is confined to finitely many types for the connected row-isometry group there has a finite-dimensional span of right translates under the subgroup generated by all of these groups. It is used in the analysis of isotypic cuspidal spaces, namely in the bounds `iSup_inf_levelInvariantSubmodule_inf_archCutSubmodule_le` and `iSup_inf_levelInvariantSubmodule_principal_inf_archCutSubmodule_le` and in `exists_rightConv_eq_of_archCutProjector`.
